      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, it seems like you've got a security policy that's a bit too eager to lock the door, even for your own services. It's like a mischievous goblin who thinks it's guarding the treasure but ends up locking everyone out. Let's tweak that SCP to allow your application roles access to S3, while still keeping the goblins at bay.\n\nFirst, you'll want to remove the blanket \"Deny\" statement and replace it with a more nuanced approach. Think of it as giving your trusted goblins (application roles) a special key to the treasure (S3 buckets) while still keeping the goblin gatekeepers (security policies) in place to watch over the rest.\n\nHere's a revised version of your SCP:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Sid\": \"DenyAllS3NonAdmin\",\n      \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n      \"Action\": \"s3:*\",\n      \"Resource\": \"*\",\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringNotEquals\": {\n          \"aws:PrincipalArn\": \"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/admin-role\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"Sid\":",
